cactus of doom wrote:
> How do I read that encryption (I know all the answers to these
> questions, but I see a lot of coded messages I'd really like to
> decipher)?

it's called rot13. Use http://www.rot13.com/ to encrypt/decrypt (the
cypher is symmetric).

Or, if you're a *nix person (including a Mac person with a fondness for
the terminal), you can use
alias rot13='tr "a-zA-Z" "n-za-mN-ZA-M"'
to define a command that will encrypt/decrypt any text you throw at it.



